      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ==================== NAVIGATION ==================== -->
<nav class="section-nav">
  <div class="container">
    <a href="#station-utilization">Station Utilization</a>
    <a href="#queue-wait-analysis">Queue &amp; Wait Times</a>
    <a href="#energy-grid-load">Energy &amp; Grid Load</a>
    <a href="#renewable-pricing">Renewables &amp; Pricing</a>
    <a href="#vehicle-charging-behavior">Vehicle Profiles</a>
    <a href="#optimization-recommendations">Recommendations</a>
  </div>
</nav>

<!-- ==================== SECTION 1: Station Utilization ==================== -->
<section class="section" id="station-utilization">
<div class="container">
  <h2 class="section-title"><span class="num">1</span> Station Utilization &amp; Demand Analysis</h2>
  <p class="section-objective">Charging demand distribution across 20 stations and two location types (Urban, Highway), identifying high-demand stations, peak utilization periods, and capacity constraints.</p>

  <div class="chart-grid">
    <div class="chart-card">
      <h3>Sessions by Location Type</h3>
      <div class="chart-wrap"><canvas id="chart-loc-sessions"></canvas></div>
    </div>
    <div class="chart-card">
      <h3>Sessions by Time Slot &amp; Location</h3>
      <div class="chart-wrap"><canvas id="chart-loc-timeslot"></canvas></div>
    </div>
    <div class="chart-card full">
      <h3>Sessions &amp; Average Demand by Station</h3>
      <div class="chart-wrap"><canvas id="chart-station-sessions" height="100"></canvas></div>
    </div>
    <div class="chart-card">
      <h3>Average Station Load by Time Slot</h3>
      <div class="chart-wrap"><canvas id="chart-load-timeslot"></canvas></div>
    </div>
    <div class="chart-card">
      <h3>Sessions by Day of Week</h3>
      <div class="chart-wrap"><canvas id="chart-dow-sessions"></canvas></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="chart-card full" style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
    <h3>Top 5 Stations by Average Charging Demand</h3>
    <table class="data-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Station</th><th>Location</th><th class="num-cell">Sessions</th><th class="num-cell">Avg Demand</th><th class="num-cell">Avg Load (kW)</th><th class="num-cell">Avg Queue</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>ST012</td><td>Urban</td><td class="num-cell">421</td><td class="num-cell">56.07</td><td class="num-cell">55.85</td><td class="num-cell">4.61</td></tr>
        <tr><td>ST003</td><td>Urban</td><td class="num-cell">431</td><td class="num-cell">55.14</td><td class="num-cell">54.92</td><td class="num-cell">4.60</td></tr>
        <tr><td>ST007</td><td>Urban</td><td class="num-cell">391</td><td class="num-cell">54.86</td><td class="num-cell">54.85</td><td class="num-cell">4.26</td></tr>
        <tr><td>ST004</td><td>Urban</td><td class="num-cell">405</td><td class="num-cell">54.50</td><td class="num-cell">54.49</td><td class="num-cell">4.53</td></tr>
        <tr><td>ST002</td><td>Highway</td><td class="num-cell">398</td><td class="num-cell">54.42</td><td class="num-cell">54.53</td><td class="num-cell">4.78</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="insight-box">
    <strong>Key Takeaway</strong>
    Urban and Highway locations are nearly equally represented (4,188 vs 4,166 sessions). Demand and load are remarkably balanced across both location types, but station load jumps from ~34.7 kW during Off-Peak to ~84.1 kW during Peak &mdash; a 2.4&times; increase. The top-demand stations (ST012, ST003, ST007) are all Urban, suggesting urban nodes experience slightly higher utilization pressure. Charger allocation across 10 charger IDs is evenly distributed (807&ndash;904 sessions each), indicating no single charger is a bottleneck.
  </div>
</div>
</section>

<!-- ==================== SECTION 2: Queue & Wait Time ==================== -->
<section class="section" id="queue-wait-analysis">
<div class="container">
  <h2 class="section-title"><span class="num">2</span> Queue Length &amp; Waiting Time Analysis</h2>
  <p class="section-objective">Queue lengths and waiting times by station, time slot, vehicle type, and traffic density to identify bottleneck patterns and quantify the customer experience impact.</p>

  <div class="chart-grid">
    <div class="chart-card">
      <h3>Waiting Time Distribution</h3>
      <div class="chart-wrap"><canvas id="chart-wait-dist"></canvas></div>
    </div>
    <div class="chart-card">
      <h3>Waiting Time Percentiles</h3>
      <div class="chart-wrap"><canvas id="chart-wait-pct"></canvas></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Heatmap: Wait Time by Location & Time Slot -->
  <div class="chart-card full" style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
    <h3>Average Waiting Time Heatmap &mdash; Location Type &times; Time Slot</h3>
    <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 120px 1fr 1fr; gap: 4px; max-width: 500px; margin: 16px auto;">
      <div class="heatmap-label"></div>
      <div class="heatmap-label">Off-Peak</div>
      <div class="heatmap-label">Peak</div>
      <div class="heatmap-label" style="text-align:right; padding-right:10px;">Highway</div>
      <div class="heatmap-cell" style="background: #dc8936;">9.63 min</div>
      <div class="heatmap-cell" style="background: #d4803a;">9.55 min</div>
      <div class="heatmap-label" style="text-align:right; padding-right:10px;">Urban</div>
      <div class="heatmap-cell" style="background: #d4803a;">9.54 min</div>
      <div class="heatmap-cell" style="background: #c8742e;">9.31 min</div>
    </div>
    <p style="text-align:center; font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--muted); margin-top:8px;">Darker = lower wait time. Range: 9.31 &ndash; 9.63 min.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- Heatmap: Queue Length by Location & Time Slot -->
  <div class="chart-card full" style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
    <h3>Average Queue Length Heatmap &mdash; Location Type &times; Time Slot</h3>
    <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 120px 1fr 1fr; gap: 4px; max-width: 500px; margin: 16px auto;">
      <div class="heatmap-label"></div>
      <div class="heatmap-label">Off-Peak</div>
      <div class="heatmap-label">Peak</div>
      <div class="heatmap-label" style="text-align:right; padding-right:10px;">Highway</div>
      <div class="heatmap-cell" style="background: #3b82f6;">4.70</div>
      <div class="heatmap-cell" style="background: #2563eb;">4.47</div>
      <div class="heatmap-label" style="text-align:right; padding-right:10px;">Urban</div>
      <div class="heatmap-cell" style="background: #3373ed;">4.60</div>
      <div class="heatmap-cell" style="background: #2969ec;">4.52</div>
    </div>
    <p style="text-align:center; font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--muted); margin-top:8px;">Darker = lower queue. Range: 4.47 &ndash; 4.70 vehicles.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="chart-grid">
    <div class="chart-card">
      <h3>Avg Waiting Time by Vehicle Type</h3>
      <div class="chart-wrap"><canvas id="chart-wait-vtype"></canvas></div>
    </div>
    <div class="chart-card">
      <h3>Avg Waiting Time by Traffic Density</h3>
      <div class="chart-wrap"><canvas id="chart-wait-traffic"></canvas></div>
    </div>
    <div class="chart-card">
      <h3>Avg Waiting Time by Day of Week</h3>
      <div class="chart-wrap"><canvas id="chart-wait-dow"></canvas></div>
    </div>
    <div class="chart-card">
      <h3>Avg Queue Length by Day of Week</h3>
      <div class="chart-wrap"><canvas id="chart-queue-dow"></canvas></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="insight-box warning">
    <strong>Key Takeaway</strong>
    Average waiting time is moderate at 9.53 minutes (median: 9 min), but 10% of sessions exceed 16 minutes and 5% exceed 18 minutes &mdash; a notable tail. Waiting times are remarkably consistent across location types, time slots, and vehicle types (range: 9.31&ndash;9.63 min), suggesting the bottleneck is systemic rather than localized. The near-zero correlation (-0.005) between queue length and waiting time indicates that wait times are driven more by charging session duration and charger availability than queue depth itself. Saturday shows the highest average queue length (4.81), warranting weekend staffing adjustments.
  </div>
