<section class="section" id="optimization-recommendations">
<div class="container">
  <h2 class="section-title"><span class="num">6</span> Optimization Insights &amp; Recommendations</h2>
  <p class="section-objective">Synthesized findings into actionable recommendations for load balancing, queue management, pricing strategy adjustments, and renewable energy maximization.</p>

  <div class="rec-grid">
    <div class="rec-card">
      <h4>1. Implement Time-of-Use Pricing to Shift Load</h4>
      <p>Current pricing (~$9.96) is flat across time slots despite a 2.4&times; load differential. Introduce a 20&ndash;30% peak surcharge and a 15&ndash;20% off-peak discount to incentivize demand shifting. Off-peak windows currently handle 62.5% of sessions &mdash; pricing incentives could push this to 70%+, reducing peak station loads from 84 kW toward the 60&ndash;70 kW range.</p>
      <span class="impact">High Impact &bull; Load Balancing</span>
    </div>
    <div class="rec-card green">
      <h4>2. Create &ldquo;Green Charging&rdquo; Windows</h4>
      <p>Renewable ratio is 39.3% during off-peak vs 29.0% during peak &mdash; and this is the strongest driver of optimization reward (r = 0.59). Introduce branded &ldquo;Green Charging&rdquo; periods with discounted rates during high-renewable off-peak windows. Promote via app notifications when renewable ratio exceeds 40%. This aligns cost savings with sustainability goals.</p>
      <span class="impact">High Impact &bull; Sustainability</span>
    </div>
    <div class="rec-card orange">
      <h4>3. Introduce Priority-Based Queue Management</h4>
      <p>Currently, priority assignment (High/Medium/Low) has no measurable effect on waiting times (9.51 min across all tiers). Implement actual priority queuing for public transit buses and high-priority commercial vehicles. Target: reduce bus wait times to &lt;7 min while keeping overall average under 10 min. This requires software changes to the queue assignment algorithm.</p>
      <span class="impact">Medium Impact &bull; Queue Optimization</span>
    </div>
    <div class="rec-card red">
      <h4>4. Address Peak Grid Stress at Capacity Ceiling</h4>
      <p>Peak station loads hit 100 kW maximum across all 20 stations &mdash; the grid ceiling. With demand growing, this leaves zero headroom. Options: (a) negotiate higher grid allocations at high-demand urban stations (ST012, ST003, ST007), (b) deploy on-site battery storage (200&ndash;400 kWh) to buffer peak loads, (c) implement smart charging that throttles low-priority sessions during grid stress events.</p>
      <span class="impact">Critical &bull; Grid Capacity</span>
    </div>
    <div class="rec-card">
      <h4>5. Optimize Charger Power Allocation</h4>
      <p>Four power tiers (7, 11, 22, 50 kW) are used in equal proportion regardless of vehicle type or urgency. Implement smart power assignment: direct 50 kW chargers to high-priority and time-sensitive sessions, reserve 7&ndash;11 kW for overnight/long-duration off-peak sessions. This reduces peak concurrency stress without adding hardware.</p>
      <span class="impact">Medium Impact &bull; Throughput</span>
    </div>
    <div class="rec-card green">
      <h4>6. Weekend Queue Staffing &amp; Capacity</h4>
      <p>Saturday shows the highest average queue length (4.81 vehicles) across the week. Consider deploying mobile charging units at high-traffic highway stations (ST013, ST002) on weekends, or enabling overflow routing to nearby lower-demand urban stations (ST007: lowest queue at 4.26). App-based wait time predictions can redistribute demand in real time.</p>
      <span class="impact">Medium Impact &bull; Customer Experience</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="insight-box" style="margin-top: 32px;">
    <strong>Implementation Priority Matrix</strong><br>
    <strong>Immediate (0&ndash;3 months):</strong> Deploy time-of-use pricing (#1) and activate priority queuing (#3) &mdash; these are software-only changes with the fastest ROI.<br>
    <strong>Near-term (3&ndash;6 months):</strong> Launch Green Charging program (#2) and smart power allocation (#5) &mdash; require app integration and charger firmware updates.<br>
    <strong>Strategic (6&ndash;12 months):</strong> Address grid ceiling (#4) and weekend capacity (#6) &mdash; require infrastructure investment and grid operator negotiations.
